<aside class="news" aria-labelledby="news-heading">
  <p class="news-label" id="news-heading">News</p>
  <article>
    <p class="news-date"><time datetime="2026-09-24">24 September 2026</time></p>
    <p>The FISCO model has been updated to reflect recent developments in the EU fiscal framework. Recent releases incorporate the Commission&rsquo;s methodology for the eligible energy spending exemptions and its updated control account presentation, including application of the &ldquo;Correction for breaks in time series&rdquo; adjustment. These updates have been made incrementally to maintain consistency with evolving EU surveillance methodologies while preserving the underlying structure of the original model.</p>
    <p>The pace and volume of changes to the surveillance framework, combined with limited and inconsistent implementation guidance, have presented a challenge to development and validation under the original project scope. Updates and guidance are provided on a voluntary, best-efforts basis. Users should exercise appropriate judgement when applying the model and be aware that some elements may require further refinement in future releases.</p>
  </article>
</aside>

<section>
  <h2>What FISCO does</h2>
  <p>FISCO is a template for IFIs to operationalise the EU’s reformed economic governance framework. It assesses both the medium-term fiscal-structural plan's compliance with Regulation (EU) 2024/1263 and its annual implementation against the agreed net expenditure path commitment and other debt, deficit and control account criteria.</p>

  <div class="card-grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Medium-Term Plan assessment</h3>
      <p>Tests the proposed net expenditure path against debt sustainability, deficit, and minimum-effort safeguards.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Implementation monitoring</h3>
      <p>Tracks annual and cumulative deviations from net expenditure plans in the control account, and flags any breaches of the 0.3% and 0.6% of GDP thresholds.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Built for IFIs</h3>
      <p>Transparent formulas, automatic data updates from Eurostat and AMECO, and a step-by-step workflow with video tutorials.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
